1
00:04:47,368 --> 00:04:53,368
When he fell into silence, movies gave him back his voice

2
00:09:34,736 --> 00:09:40,736
Life, Animated is a documentary film directed by Roger Ross Williams.

3
00:14:22,105 --> 00:14:28,105
At three years old, a chatty, energetic little boy named Owen Suskind ceased
to speak, disappearing into autism with apparently no way out.

4
00:19:09,473 --> 00:19:15,473
Almost four years passed and the only stimuli that
engaged Owen were Disney films.

5
00:23:56,842 --> 00:24:02,842
Then one day, his father donned a puppet—Iago, the wisecracking parrot
from Aladdin—and asked “what’s it like to be you?” And poof!

6
00:28:44,210 --> 00:28:50,210
Owen replied, with dialogue from the movie.

7
00:33:31,578 --> 00:33:37,578
Life, Animated tells the remarkable story of how Owen found in Disney animation a
pathway to language and a framework for making sense of the world.

8
00:38:18,947 --> 00:38:24,947
Himself, played by Owen Suskind.

9
00:43:06,315 --> 00:43:12,315
Himself, played by Ron Suskind.

10
00:47:53,684 --> 00:47:59,684
Himself, played by Jonathan Freeman.

11
00:52:41,052 --> 00:52:47,052
Himself, played by Gilbert Gottfried.

12
00:57:28,421 --> 00:57:34,421
Life, Animated is a 2016  American independent
documentary film by director Roger Ross Williams.

13
01:02:15,789 --> 01:02:21,789
It is co-produced by Williams with Julie Goldman,
Carolyn Hepburn and Christopher Clements.

14
01:07:03,157 --> 01:07:09,157
Life, Animated is based on journalist Ron Suskind's 2014 book Life, Animated: A Story of Sidekicks, Heroes, and Autism, which tells the story of his son,
Owen Suskind, who struggles with autism and learned how to communicate with the outside world through his love of Disney animated films.

15
01:11:50,526 --> 01:11:56,526
Upon its release, the film received generally positive reviews from critics and won numerous awards including
the Sundance Film Festival award for Best Direction and the Special Achievement Annie Award.

16
01:16:37,894 --> 01:16:43,894
It was also nominated for the Academy Award for Best Documentary Feature Film
category at the 89th Academy Awards, but lost to O.J.: Made in America.

17
01:21:25,263 --> 01:21:31,263
The film explores themes of autism, candid,
inspirational, awestruck, empathetic.

18
01:26:12,631 --> 01:26:18,631
The tone is uplifting.
